From 39ec2f8e74cc0f02d160c28aaf8d87caa877e98f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 19:54:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 35/41] arm64: configs: rename QFPROM symbol for v6.1+ Kconfig

CONFIG_QCOM_QFPROM is the v6.0-era symbol name; this tree's
drivers/nvmem/Kconfig only knows it as NVMEM_QCOM_QFPROM (renamed
upstream for v6.1). olddefconfig was silently dropping the unknown
symbol -- another instance of the QFPROM-class trap already documented
in docs/BUILD-RUNBOOK.md, this time on the symbol the trap is named
after. Caught by the runbook's mandatory 13-symbol sanity grep after
`make taimen_defconfig`, which read 12 instead of 13 before this fix.

The driver itself is unchanged and available on this tree
(ARCH_QCOM + HAS_IOMEM, same as v6.0); only the Kconfig symbol moved.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
index 3ffd939978de..a47709a009fb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
@@ -4886,7 +4886,7 @@ CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_DEVICES="binder,hwbinder,vndbinder,anbox-binder,anbox-hwbi
 # CONFIG_DAX is not set
 CONFIG_NVMEM=y
 CONFIG_NVMEM_SYSFS=y
-CONFIG_QCOM_QFPROM=y
+CONFIG_NVMEM_QCOM_QFPROM=y
 # CONFIG_NVMEM_SPMI_SDAM is not set
 # CONFIG_NVMEM_RMEM is not set
 
